"comparison": "JPM and GS both describe a comprehensive allocation approach where all revenues, expenses, and assets are assigned to segments to reflect stand-alone performance. JPM reports that segment results involve 'the allocation of certain income and expense items' to present segments as stand-alone businesses. GS mirrors this by stating, 'The firm fully allocates its revenues, expenses, assets and shareholders' equity to the firm's three business segments.' Furthermore, both acknowledge the judgment involved in these allocations; JPM states the 'Firm periodically assesses the assumptions, methodologies and reporting classifications,' while GS admits that 'Due to the integrated nature of these segments, estimates and judgments are made in allocating these assets, revenues and expenses.'",
